# ALLOWLIST. Ignore everything, then permit exactly what the image needs.
#
# The usual default (permit everything, ignore a few folders) is how a .venv, a
# .git directory, a .env with a secret, or a file of personal addresses ends up
# inside an image. With an allowlist, a new file is OUT of the image until someone
# deliberately lets it in.
*

# the pinned serving dependencies
!requirements/serve.txt

# the serving code: only what the API imports. NOT thikana/training (needs pandas)
!thikana/__init__.py
!thikana/schema.py
!thikana/text.py
!thikana/features.py
!thikana/model.py
!thikana/api/
!thikana/web/

# the production model and its sidecar (vocabulary + feature flags). The models/
# folder is gitignored, so it must be built first: python -m thikana.training.train_all
!models/crf_all_district_memory_vocab.crfsuite
!models/crf_all_district_memory_vocab.json

# bytecode never ships, even from inside an allowed folder
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
